    "long_instructions": "# Interactive Data App\r\n\r\n1. **Create Interactive Filters and Sorting:** Write functions for at least two filters and one sorting option.\r\n\r\n   - **Note:** Create a new list inside your function (\"copy, don't mutate\") rather than changing the original dataset.\r\n\r\n2. **Add User Controls:** Add a Reset button to reload the original data, an Undo button that removes the last filter applied, an active filter display, and a label that updates dynamically, such as `Showing 5 results`.\r\n\r\n3. **Consult AI:** Use AI to generate test cases and debug your logic. You might ask:\r\n   - *What test cases should I try for my filters, sorting, Reset, and Undo buttons?*\r\n   - *Why does my filtered list return zero results?*\r\n   - *How do I sort an array of objects alphabetically by a specific property?*\r\n\r\n4. **Test Your Code:** Try each filter, combine filters, test sorting, and check Reset and Undo. Also test edge cases, such as missing values or filters with zero results. Make any revisions to your code as needed.",
